    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1958-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(f(x)=\\frac{x+1}{x-1}.\\) Then \\[ \\begin{aligned} f(f(x)) &=\\frac{\\frac{x+1}{x-1}+1} {\\frac{x+1}{x-1}-1}\\\\ &=\\frac{\\frac{2x}{x-1}}{\\frac{2}{x-1}} =x. \\end{aligned} \\] At \\(x=\\frac{1}{2},\\) the value is \\(\\frac{1}{2},\\) which is not listed.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Let \\(f(x)=\\frac{x+1}{x-1}\\) and simplify \\(f(f(x))\\)",
        "Combine the numerator and denominator of the composed fraction separately"
      ],
